+{"schemaVersion":"1","kind":"observation","id":"obs_01M2H1BMCQYAYTWGP8BKYXCKFY","recordedAt":"2026-09-14T21:59:48Z","companyId":"example-co","controlIds":["sebi-cscrf-2024:ID.AM.S5"],"title":"classification-conflict: 4 in onfinance-db-model-master","description":"Four classification-conflict gaps in db-models-mongodb: (1) target db-models-mongodb.default.user.user_debank_url: declared as a URLField (looks like a plain profile link), but a DeBank profile URL carries the user's crypto wallet address, which identifies the user's financial account and holdings; took the stricter class financial + spdi + pii. (2) target db-models-mongodb.default.secrets: zerodha_username could be a plain login name (restricted) or the Zerodha client ID / UCC (pii): classified restricted + pii. apiSecrets and accessToken could be application secrets (restricted) or password-equivalent trading-account credentials (spdi under the SPDI Rules 2011 'passwords or hashes'): classified restricted + spdi + pii. apiKey stays restricted only as a Kite Connect app identifier. user.user_binance_auth_creds (DynamicField) has the same conflict and was classified restricted + financial + spdi + pii. (3) target db-models-mongodb.default.user.profile_answers: untyped DynamicField that could be generic onboarding preferences (confidential) or the user's self-reported profile/risk answers (personal data); took the stricter class confidential + pii, pending a runtime sample by runtime-probe-datapipeline. The same untyped-structure conflict applies to user.user_binance_auth_creds (classified restricted + financial + spdi + pii) and to entity.fundamental_analysis / technical_analysis / important_links (kept internal as entity analytics, not personal data). (4) target db-models-mongodb: applications/db-models/env/dev.json declares dataClassification ['internal'], but the models this application ships define pii, spdi (user_password, zerodha_password, zerodha_2fa, trading-account tokens) and financial (portfolio