+{"schemaVersion":"1","kind":"observation","id":"obs_01M2H1VF3NXP9G2FQRS3M7VTT2","recordedAt":"2026-09-14T21:59:48Z","companyId":"example-co","controlIds":["sebi-cscrf-2024:PR.AA.S9","cert-in-directions-2022:Dir-iv","dpdp-rules-2025:6(1)(e)","sebi-cscrf-2024:ID.AM.S5"],"title":"log-retention-below-180d: mcp-gateway.mongodb-mcp-server.disk-logs in mongodb-mcp-server","description":"Target mcp-gateway.mongodb-mcp-server.disk-logs: The server's own on-disk logger keeps tool-call and server logs for only 30 days (MongoLogManager retentionDays: 30, src/common/logging/diskLogger.ts:23) under ~/.mongodb/mongodb-mcp/.app-logs (src/common/config/configUtils.ts:49), below cert-in-directions-2022 Dir-iv logRetentionDays 180 and far below sebi-cscrf-2024 PR.AA.S9's two years for critical-system user access logs; mcp-gateway implements the order-routing critical function and these logs record AI-agent tool calls against client data. The shipped Dockerfiles mitigate by defaulting MDB_MCP_LOGGERS=stderr,mcp (Dockerfile:7, deploy/aws/Dockerfile:12), but the library default enables the disk logger (src/common/config/userConfig.ts:58), the ENV is overridable per deployment, and the dev environment declares logsRetentionDays 30 itself (applications/mcp-gateway/env/dev.json:15). Confirm prod keeps the disk logger off and that stderr reaches the SIEM with >=180 days (prod env declares 365). Regulatory basis: cert-in-directions-2022 Dir-iv (180-day ICT system logs within India), sebi-cscrf-2024 PR.AA.S9 (two-year user access logs for critical systems), dpdp-rules-2025 6(1)(e) (retain logs and personal data for one year), iso-27001-2022 A.8.15 (cited by the gap but dropped from controlIds: no iso-27001-2022 catalog file exists in regulatory-catalogs, so no control record can be created for it).","methods":["refresh-metastore"],"subjects":[{"type":"repo","appId":"mcp-gateway","repoId":"mongodb-mcp-server"}],"collectedAt":"2026-09-14T21:59:48Z","result":"not-satisfied","evidence":[{"type":"